    year = {2026},
    pages = {213-241},
    abstract = {This chapter examines how social media can transform entrepreneurship education by enhancing student engagement and entrepreneurial skill development. It introduces the SCALE Framework—Social Exposure, Content Curation, Active Participation, Learning Reflection, and Entrepreneurial Application—grounded in experiential learning, social learning, self-determination theory, and connectivism. The chapter highlights the educational potential of platforms such as Instagram, YouTube, and LinkedIn, addresses challenges including AI-augmented content, algorithmic literacy, and digital wellbeing, and argues that purposeful social media integration can bridge the gap between academic learning and entrepreneurial practice.},
