    journal = {Journal of Environmental Spectrum},
    doi = {10.66567/jykc3p43},
    year = {2025},
    abstract = {Social media (SM) has transformed the communication landscape for Higher Education, thereby redefining Education. SM tools provide an innovative pedagogical approach to curriculum delivery and student engagement. However, the extent of use of SM platforms by built environment students relating to their discipline remains unknown. This study assessed the SM platforms used by built environment students. The study adopted a quantitative approach as the research design. A structured questionnaire was used to obtain information regarding SM platforms popular amongst built environment students (Architecture, Building, Civil Engineering, and Quantity Surveying) in Ahmadu Bello University (ABU) Zaria. The findings from the study revealed WhatsApp to be the most popular platform among Generation Z students (born between 1995 and 2010) in the built environment, followed by the media-sharing platforms Instagram and YouTube. Hence, the study concludes that built environment students do not understand effectively using SM within their discipline. The study further recommends that built environment students be properly guided on which and how SM can enhance their overall performance and give them the optimum visibility after graduation.},
