    year = {2026},
    pages = {69–100},
    abstract = {The purpose of this study is to investigate the use of AI for the production and monetization of cyberliterature from the perspective of educational transformation 7.0 using trifecta models. Specifically in literature lessons, this study seeks to enhance student engagement, creativity, and monetization opportunities using AI. The researchers used a survey design to conduct a quantitative study, sending questionnaires to 125 university students in Indonesia. The selected sample included representatives from Universitas Muhammadiyah Purwokerto, Universitas Al Asyariah Mandar, and the State Islamic Institute of Madura. The study analyzed responses about the use of AI tools for writing, enhancing creativity, and monetizing cyberliterature using descriptive statistics. The study found that students generally understand AI tools and their potential applications in creative writing. There are still a few students who monetize their writing using sites like Webtoon or Instagram, although many have used AI to write and are aware that their cyberliterature work can be monetized. This study yields mixed results on AI's ability to foster creativity. This study shows how AI can help people from all backgrounds understand and enjoy literature in our increasingly interconnected society. The long-term impact of AI-enhanced pedagogical resources on student interest and originality should be the subject of future study.},
